\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces An example of min-sum decoding on the BEC using the (3,2) regular LDPC code. Note that,for BEC, $\phi \left (\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{j'} \phi (\beta _{j'i})\right )$ is 0 or $\infty $ exactly when $min_{j'} \beta _{j'i}$ is 0 or $\infty $, respectively. Note also that this is equivalent to the iterative erasure filling algorithm.}}{15}{}\protected@file@percent }
